            <ArticleTitle>[Application of continuous sutures for nasal septum after septoplasty].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>381-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To investigate the efficacy and safety of nasal septal suture in septoplasty.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Sixty patients who had undergone septoplasty were allocated into two groups: packing group and suturing group. Post-operative signs and symptoms (visual analogue scale) were compared between the two groups.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The patients of packing group experienced significantly more postoperative pain, epiphora, tinnitus, ear fullness, sleep disturbance and nasal congestion(P&lt;0. 05). No statistically significant difference between two groups in hemorrhage (P&gt;0. 05).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Nasal septum continuous suture is a feasible method to replace nasal packing after septoplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
